us_prri: religion by county, PRRI Census of American Religion
  excluding mL9BH and the diversity_index column (The Religious Diversity Index, By County -- a 0-1 concentration score rather than a percentage of anybody)
  d76SP v7: https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/d76SP/7/dataset.csv
  3142 counties, data year 2024
  CLuyf v4: https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/CLuyf/4/dataset.csv
  cross-check: CLuyf matches d76SP across 3142 counties
  collapse: PRRI's 11 Christian categories all land in ['Catholicism', "Jehovah's Witnesses", 'Latter-day Saints', 'Orthodoxy', 'Protestantism']
  population: median 0.74 of the ACS resident count (an adult base, as expected)
  sums: worst county 4.7pp from 100, median 0.1pp
    furthest from 100 -- 37183 Wake County, NC 95.3%; 36081 Queens County, NY 96.1%; 25017 Middlesex County, MA 97.4%; 06071 San Bernardino County, CA 97.4%; 48439 Tarrant County, TX 98.0%
  national roll-up by node: Protestantism 44.7%, No religion 23.1%, Catholicism 22.0%, Other religions 1.8%, Judaism 1.8%, Latter-day Saints 1.8%, Buddhism 1.0%, Islam 1.0%, Jehovah's Witnesses 0.9%, Hinduism 0.8%, Orthodoxy 0.6%
